#41034
the Hidden Tunnels Below the Rue de Belleville~
The hidden tunnels beneath the Rue de Belleville have been patched with
masonry from several different jobs. Pale brick interrupts older stone, and
one broad repair has swallowed the lower half of a faded wall mark. A shallow
drainage line follows the floor before bending out of the immediate view. The
city feels present above as pressure and distance, reduced here to damp joints
and enclosed air.`x
